Subject: usp-pa-vendor-rdk: terminate LCM_Handle_Table_Changes property scan

LCM_Handle_Table_Changes() walks the properties of an incoming rbus event
looking for one named "rowName".  The while(prop != NULL) loop has no
iterator advance:

    while (prop != NULL) {
        const char * prop_name = rbusProperty_GetName(prop);
        rbusValue_t val = rbusProperty_GetValue(prop);
        if (strcmp("rowName", prop_name) == 0) {
            rowName = rbusValue_GetString(val, NULL);
            break;
        }
        /* missing: prop = rbusProperty_GetNext(prop); */
    }

If the first property of the event isn't "rowName", the loop pins the same
prop forever — pegging obuspa's rbus event-callback thread at 100% CPU as
soon as timingila publishes any Device.SoftwareModules.* table-change.

Symptom observed:
    $ ps -o pid,pcpu -C obuspa
       PID  %CPU
      4881   136

Fix: advance the iterator at the end of the loop body, matching the
otherwise-identical loop at line 124 of the same file.

Trivial single-line fix; suitable for an upstream PR to
github.com/rdkcentral/usp-pa-vendor-rdk.
---
 lcm_rbus_datamodel.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/lcm_rbus_datamodel.c b/lcm_rbus_datamodel.c
--- a/lcm_rbus_datamodel.c
+++ b/lcm_rbus_datamodel.c
@@ -293,6 +293,7 @@ static void LCM_Handle_Table_Changes(__attribute((unused)) rbusHandle_t handle,
             rowName = rbusValue_GetString(val,NULL);
             break;
         }
+        prop = rbusProperty_GetNext(prop);
     }

     if (rowName == NULL) { return; }    //exit early if this is null as the required string was not found
